      "dom_id": "question-29342",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{32{a}^{7}{b}^{8}}$ given that $a\\ge 0.$",
      "worked_solution": "We first write $32{a}^{7}{b}^{8}$ as the product $16{a}^{6}{b}^{8}\\cdot 2a$ which contains a perfect square $(16{a}^{6}{b}^{8}).$ Then, we separate the product into two separate radicals, one of which can be simplified:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{32{a}^{7}{b}^{8}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{16{a}^{6}{b}^{8}\\cdot 2a} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(4{a}^{3}{b}^{4})^{2}\\cdot 2a} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(4{a}^{3}{b}^{4})^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & = \\\\ |4{a}^{3}{b}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & = \\\\ |4|\\cdot |{a}^{3}|\\cdot |{b}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & = \\\\ 4\\cdot |{a}^{3}|\\cdot |{b}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA number raised to the power of four is always positive or zero, and the absolute value of any positive (or zero) number is itself, so we have that $|{b}^{4}|={b}^{4}$ and $|{a}^{3}|={a}^{3}.$ Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot |{a}^{3}|\\cdot |{b}^{4}|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & = \\\\ 4\\cdot {a}^{3}\\cdot {b}^{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & = \\\\ 4{a}^{3}{b}^{4}\\sqrt{2a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
